error[L0363]: macro code ran too many steps
    --> expand/macro_steps_charge_hidden_module_definitions.knv:6013:42
     |
6013 |                   (defn main () (println (lists))))
     |                                          ^^^^^^^ this call passed 10000 macro steps
     |
     = note: the macro calls in one top-level form run at most 10000 steps: a function call or a `recur` costs one step per expression of the body it runs, an `expand-call` costs 64 and one per form it returns, a closure costs one step and one per binding in scope, and a built-in costs one step per list item it copies or reads and one for every 16 bytes of text it reads, and `closest-name` one step for each pair of bytes it compares between the name and the candidates
     = help: make the macro stop, or wrap the top-level form in `(with-macro-steps 30000000 ...)`
